# Agent guide — goenvoy

`goenvoy` = multi-module monorepo, pure-stdlib Go HTTP-API clients (arr stack, metadata, download clients, media servers, anime). Module path `github.com/golusoris/goenvoy/<category>/<service>`, tag `<category>/<service>/vX.Y.Z`. Layout: [README.md](../../README.md). Full contract: [docs/principles.md](../../docs/principles.md). Read per-category `AGENTS.md` for area touched.

## Hard rules

1. Stdlib imports only (ADR-0001); `depguard` enforces. Dependency idea -> ADR first, never a suggestion.
2. Constructor `New(baseURL, apiKey string, opts ...Option) (*Client, error)`, functional options `With*`; exceptions (OAuth2 device code, public-key-only) live in module `AGENTS.md`.
3. Every I/O method: `context.Context` first.
4. Every module: `APIError` (status, message, body) implementing `error`.
5. Every response body closed (`defer resp.Body.Close()`); `bodyclose` enforces.
6. Errors wrap `fmt.Errorf("<module>: <op>: %w", err)`; `wrapcheck` enforces.
7. No secret (API key, bearer, refresh token) in errors, wrapped errors, fixtures.
8. Per module per merged commit: 0 lint, 0 gosec, 0 govulncheck, race green, coverage >= 70%. `//nolint` needs same-line reason.
9. Breaking public API: `Migration:` footer, before/after Go snippets; `apidiff` vs last tag.
10. User input in URL paths -> `url.PathEscape`.
11. Comments: one-line `// Why:` only. No new Markdown docs unless asked.
12. Tests: `httptest` only, never live APIs. New method -> table-driven test + runnable godoc example.

## CI gates

Per module: `golangci-lint run` (`.golangci.yml`), `gosec` (SARIF), `govulncheck`, `go test -race -count=1 -cover`, `apidiff`, `go vet`, `go build`. Repo-wide: Conventional Commits PR title, CodeQL (`security-extended,security-and-quality`), OSSF Scorecard.

## Skills, hooks

Skills in `.claude/skills/`: `add-service-client`, `add-service-method`, `bump-module`, `release-module`, `audit-service-docs`.

Hooks in `.claude/hooks/`: `guard-bash.sh` blocks hook-skip and unsigned-commit flags, force-push to main, `rm -rf .git` / `.workingdir*`; `guard-go-edit.sh` blocks non-stdlib imports, unjustified `InsecureSkipVerify` / `//nolint`, live-API URLs in tests; `format-go-write.sh` runs `gofumpt` + `gci`.

## Per-commit doc-sync

- Module conventions changed -> `<module>/AGENTS.md`.
- Upstream API moved -> `docs/upstream/<service>.md` (doc URL, target version, last-verified date; check it before new method).
- No hand edit of `CHANGELOG.md`; release-please writes notes from Conventional Commit subject.
- Significant audit finding fixed, confirmed or ruled out -> private `.workingdir/STATE.md`.
- Hardening pass ships full set: code fixes, agent/tooling drift, CI/local-gate parity, upstream-doc refresh, verification summary.
